# Third-party executables packaged in this APK

yog-android itself is MIT-licensed (see LICENSE). Beyond its Rust
dependencies — whose licences are enumerated exhaustively by `cargo deny`
against the committed `Cargo.lock` — the APK carries two third-party
EXECUTABLES, one per supported ABI, under `lib/<abi>/` in the archive and
`nativeLibraryDir` on the device. They are built from unmodified upstream
source by `scripts/natives.sh`, pinned by version and SHA-256 in the
`Makefile`, and nothing of them is vendored into this repository.

This file is that disclosure. It is written by hand because a licence is a
statement to a person, and the sizes are here because an APK's size is a cost
somebody pays on a phone.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## curl — packaged as `libcurl_bin.so`, spent as `curl`

  Version   8.11.1
  Source    https://curl.se/download/curl-8.11.1.tar.xz
  Licence   curl (MIT/X derivative) — https://curl.se/docs/copyright.html
  Size      about 5.5 MB per ABI, stripped

Linked statically against OpenSSL below and dynamically against bionic
(`libc`, `libm`, `libdl` — the libraries Android guarantees). Built with no
CA bundle and no CA path of its own: the app concatenates the device's own
trusted roots into one PEM at every launch and the shell tool points
`SSL_CERT_FILE` at it, so the trust store is the platform's.

Copyright (c) 1996 - 2024, Daniel Stenberg, and many contributors.

