## busybox — packaged as `libbusybox_bin.so`, spent as `busybox`

  Version   1.36.1
  Source    https://busybox.net/downloads/busybox-1.36.1.tar.bz2
  Licence   GNU General Public License, version 2 ONLY (GPL-2.0-only)
            https://busybox.net/license.html
  Size      about 240 KB per ABI, stripped

Copyright (C) 1998-2023 Erik Andersen, Rob Landley, Denys Vlasenko and others.

**The GPL-2.0 obligation, and how it is met.** The busybox in this APK is
built from the unmodified upstream tarball named above, whose SHA-256 is
pinned in the `Makefile`; the applet set is `scripts/busybox-applets.conf` and
the complete build recipe is `scripts/natives.sh`. Those three files plus the
public tarball are the complete corresponding source for the binary that
ships, and this repository is public. No busybox source is modified, and no
busybox code is linked into yog-android's own binary — it is a separate
executable in the same archive.

**No TLS is compiled into it.** `CONFIG_FEATURE_WGET_HTTPS` (busybox's own
small TLS) does not verify certificates, so `busybox wget` here speaks plain
http and `curl` is the one that does https. The shell tool's description says
so, because a client that appears to do TLS and does not verify is worse than
one that says it cannot.
